  "closed_findings": [
    {
      "id": "local_map_load_authorization",
      "status": "closed_in_reviewed_source",
      "resolution": "The producer and offline builder permit local LOAD inputs only from actually emitted compile-database outputs, STATIC_LIBRARY artifacts reachable from the actual stage ELF target in the fresh codemodel-v2 dependency graph, and the exact NonSecure secure-import object. Unrelated local LOAD files are rejected; no second hardcoded local library registry is introduced."
    },
    {
      "id": "external_library_after_to_inventory_mix",
      "status": "closed_in_reviewed_source",
      "resolution": "The three ABI-selected external libraries are independently selected, copied and identity-locked before configure/build. Original and retained library observations are compared after build. Final selected inventory rows are bound to the complete after observation, and offline reconstruction checks before/after size, SHA256 and mode relationships."
    },
    {
      "id": "typed_report_identity_overwrite",
      "status": "closed_in_reviewed_source",
      "resolution": "Retained history cannot replace a selected typed report identity with different size or SHA256 before the selected row is updated."
    },
    {
      "id": "metadata_read_budget_order",
      "status": "closed_in_reviewed_source",
      "resolution": "The metadata cache cumulative-size budget is checked before reading the next metadata member."
    },
    {
      "id": "context_then_report_rewrite",
      "status": "closed_in_reviewed_source",
      "resolution": "The original successful report is published once, the context is validated and published last, and the successful opt-in path does not rewrite that report after context publication."
    }
  ],
  "additional_source_observations": [
    "The CMake graph parser binds the index and every used JSON reply to the exact stage reply directory; rejects unsafe reply names, duplicate IDs/reply filenames, missing dependencies, dependency cycles, depth overflow and artifact escapes; requires the exact stage executable image and derives reachable static artifacts.",
    "Capture retains the exact visited File API reply identities. Offline rebuilding requires the same complete visited set and recomputes the same allowed local/external LOAD union from retained data.",
    "All seven tools are captured and compared before/after. Only explicitly pinned live nm and objdump readers may inspect retained ELF/import bytes; archived commands, compilers and paths remain data.",
    "CI requests capture before configure, seals under RUNNER_TEMP, performs independently anchored verification, and only then copies the opaque archive and outer manifest to the upload tree. Verification failure does not publish that verified-artifact tree; always-on raw evidence and execution identity remain preserved.",
    "Archive bounds and strict typed role/member union remain intact in the reviewed source. The outer manifest SHA256 remains the caller-supplied offline trust anchor; self-rehashing does not establish builder authenticity."
  ],
